{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And when the morning dawned.</b> As the Targum renders: וּדְחִיקוּ — they pressed him." "<b>Are there any.</b> Those who are ready for you in the house to rescue them. And some say this too is a valid settlement of the verse." "<b>You will be swept away.</b> It means 'annihilated' — as in ״עַד תֹּם כָּל הַדּוֹר״ (Deuteronomy 2), which is translated ״עַד דְּסַף כָּל דָּרָא״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:26.984893886Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}